private <T> T idempotent(String endpoint, String requestId, Object request, Class<T> type, Supplier<T> action) {
    String fingerprint = fingerprint(requestId, request);
    Optional<IdempotencyRow> existing = repo.findIdempotency(requestId);
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        IdempotencyRow rec = existing.get();
        if (!rec.fingerprint().equals(fingerprint)) {
            throw ApiException.conflict("相同 requestId 携带不同业务参数，拒绝受理");
        }
        return readValue(rec.responseBody(), type);
    }
    T result = action.get();
    try {
        repo.insertIdempotency(requestId, endpoint, fingerprint, writeValue(result), now());
    } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
        IdempotencyRow rec = repo.findIdempotency(requestId).orElseThrow(...);
        if (!rec.fingerprint().equals(fingerprint)) throw conflict;
        return readValue(rec.responseBody(), type);
    }
    return result;
}
```

Wait — issue: if action.get() succeeds and insertIdempotency throws DuplicateKeyException due to concurrent tx, catching and returning stored response is fine, but our own business writes (from action) also committed — for declare with same requestId+params concurrently, both txs would insert batch → second gets DuplicateKeyException on batch_no inside action → that propagates as error... Hmm. Concurrent identical declares: both pass idempotency check (no record yet), both try insertBatch with same batch_no → one succeeds, other gets DuplicateKeyException → we should translate to: re-read idempotency (the winner will have inserted record upon commit) and return stored response. But timing: loser's insertBatch fails immediately on unique constraint? In H2 with concurrent txs, the second insert blocks until first commits, then throws duplicate key. At that point winner's tx committed including idempotency record. So catch DuplicateKeyException around the whole action+insert sequence:

